# TradeSimple v1 — Cursor AI Handoff Rules

## Project Identity
TradeSimple is a policy-to-markets intelligence terminal. It traces US congressional bills,
lobbying filings, federal contracts, and government appointments to publicly traded tickers —
in plain English, before headlines. It is NOT a brokerage. Paper trading is a demo feature only.

## Critical Architecture Rules — Read Before Touching Anything

### Zero npm dependencies (intentional, do not break)
The entire server runs on Node.js built-ins: `http`, `fs`, `crypto`, `path`, `child_process`.
No Express, no Axios, no ORM. Adding an npm dep requires explicit discussion with the founder.
The client is also dependency-free vanilla JS (no React, Vue, Vite, bundler).

### File layout
```
server.mjs          — 9,000+ line god file: HTTP server, routing, all API handlers, auth, data fetching
public/app.js       — 8,000+ line god file: all client-side state, rendering, AI chat, charts
index.html          — Landing page at repo root (public, no auth)
public/dashboard.html — Dashboard shell (requires session)
public/charts.js    — Vanilla JS charting library (TSCharts)
ai-brain.mjs        — All Anthropic AI features: thesis, scorecard, lobby map, EDGAR, chart labels
scripts/yf_bridge.py — Python sidecar for yfinance market data fallback
data/               — Seed JSON/JSONL files (bills, lobbying, contracts, paper accounts, waitlist)
src/lib/supabase.mjs — Zero-dep Supabase REST client (server-side only)
```

### Module system
`"type": "module"` in package.json — everything is ESM. Use `import`/`export`, NOT `require`.
Server entry: `node server.mjs`. Start command: `npm run dev` (port 3000).

### Data flow
1. `server.mjs` seeds POLICY_BILLS from `data/bills-seed.json` at startup
2. Market data: Finnhub (live) → yfinance Python sidecar → Yahoo HTTP → static fallback
3. Auth: HMAC-signed session cookie (`ts_session`). Google OAuth + Apple OAuth + Demo mode
4. Paper trading: stored in `data/paper-accounts.json` (flat JSON, write-locked via `fileLock` Map)
5. AI: server-side proxy to Anthropic (`/api/research/ask`) + BYOK browser-direct fallback

### Session & auth model
- `AUTH_SECRET` env var signs session cookies. Default "dev-only-secret" must be overridden in prod.
- Demo sessions use a unique `demo-{8-hex-chars}` ID per visitor (NOT shared "demo-user").
- `getSession(req)` → `{ user: { id, name, email, picture, provider } }` or null
- All `/api/*` routes require a valid session EXCEPT: `/api/config`, `/api/landing-quotes`,
  `/api/session`, `/api/waitlist`, `/api/share/*`, `/api/ai/*`

### Paper accounts
- Stored in `data/paper-accounts.json` as `{ [userId]: { cash, positions, orders, theses, funds } }`
- Write via `writePaperStore()` which uses `fileLock` Map to prevent concurrent write corruption
- Demo accounts keyed by `demo-{uuid}` — each visitor gets their own isolated paper account
- Starting cash: `PAPER_STARTING_CASH` (default $100,000)

### AI configuration
- `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` env var controls server-side AI. When absent, local fallback answers are served.
- Model is LOCKED server-side to `process.env.ANTHROPIC_MODEL || "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001"`.
  Clients CANNOT override the model via request body (security hardening applied 2026-05-29).
- Rate limiting: `checkResearchRateLimit(userId)` — 10 req/min per user (configurable via env).
- BYOK (Bring Your Own Key): user can enter their own Anthropic/OpenAI/Gemini key in the UI.
  Stored in `state.byok` client-side only, never sent to the server.
- `/api/research/ask` POST endpoint: `{ billId?, question?, prompt?, message? }`

### Rendering patterns (client)
- All rendering is direct DOM manipulation or `innerHTML` template literals. No virtual DOM.
- Global state: `state` object in app.js. Mutate carefully — no reactivity system.
- Event delegation used for dynamically rendered buttons (data-ask-why, data-methodology-bill,
  data-show-view attributes) — see `setupLegisCardDelegation()`.
- `renderBills()` has a 200ms debounce on filter input to prevent excessive DOM rebuilds.
- `$()` is shorthand for `document.querySelector()` (defined at bottom of app.js).

### Security headers
`BASE_SECURITY_HEADERS` in server.mjs contains: `x-content-type-options`, `x-frame-options`,
`referrer-policy`, `permissions-policy`, `content-security-policy`.

### Known god-file pattern
Both server.mjs and app.js are intentionally kept as single files during v1 to minimize deployment
complexity. Do NOT split into modules without founder sign-off. Work within the existing structure.

