## Environment Variables (`.env.local`)
```
AUTH_SECRET=<random-32-char-string>          # Required in production
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<key>                      # Required for AI features
FINNHUB_API_KEY=<key>                        # Required for live market data
CONGRESS_API_KEY=<key>                       # Optional: live bill data from Congress.gov
SENATE_LDA_API_KEY=<key>                     # Optional: live lobbying from Senate LDA
ALPACA_API_KEY_ID=<key>                      # Optional: Alpaca paper/live broker
ALPACA_API_SECRET_KEY=<key>                  # Optional: Alpaca paper/live broker
ALLOW_LIVE_TRADING=false                     # Safety gate — never set true without full audit
PORT=3000
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
```

---

## Coding Conventions

### Server (server.mjs)
- All handlers: `async function handlerName(req, res, session?, ...args)`
- JSON responses: `sendJson(res, statusCode, object)`
- Text responses: `sendText(res, statusCode, string)`
- Redirects: `redirect(res, url)`
- Error format: `{ error: "snake_case_code", message?: "human readable" }`
- Fetch with timeout: `fetchWithTimeout(url, init, timeoutMs)` (wraps native fetch)
- HTML escape: `escapeHtmlText(str)` for text nodes, `escapeHtml(str)` for attributes
- Never use `console.log` in hot paths — use `console.warn` / `console.error` only

### Client (app.js)
- Template literals for HTML — always escape user-derived content with `escapeHtml()`
- State reads: `state.quotes`, `state.account`, `state.config`, `state.lobbying`, etc.
- State writes: direct mutation then call the specific render function (no global re-render)
- Async data fetch: `fetchJson(url, init?)` — throws on non-ok response
- Money formatting: `money(value)`, `compactMoney(value)`
- Never use `eval()` or `innerHTML` with unescaped user input

---

## Deployment
- Single process: `node server.mjs`
- No build step — static files served directly from `public/`
- Python dependency: `pip install yfinance` for market data fallback (optional but recommended)
- Data dir: `data/` must be writable at runtime
- Recommended: run behind nginx/Cloudflare for TLS and IP header forwarding
